WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.152
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.422 --> 00:49.382
There's a reason you're still alive.

3
00:49.466 --> 00:50.925
What are you saying?

4
00:51.009 --> 00:55.013
For 20 years, I prepared for this very moment.

5
00:55.096 --> 00:57.974
How could you be so sure that this day would come?

6
00:58.058 --> 00:59.601
That I'd still keep our promise?

7
01:00.185 --> 01:01.144
Our plans.

8
01:01.227 --> 01:04.606
I was slowly preparing this for your return.

9
01:08.234 --> 01:09.903
Don't waste your pain.

10
01:09.986 --> 01:12.322
Make it your reason to fight.

11
01:12.405 --> 01:15.784
Let's help each other. While you seek justice,

12
01:15.867 --> 01:17.702
I will help you live your life again.

13
01:19.704 --> 01:22.916
If someone is making a move around Mikoy and Chiara,

14
01:22.999 --> 01:24.250
we can't rule out

15
01:24.334 --> 01:26.795
that they're connected to La Concordat.

16
01:32.383 --> 01:34.677
We don't know yet. No assumptions.

17
01:34.761 --> 01:35.595
We need facts.

18
01:38.598 --> 01:42.060
Mario. Some information came in at the agency.

19
01:42.143 --> 01:42.977
It's not verified yet.

20
01:43.061 --> 01:45.939
So I can't give you the details.

21
01:46.523 --> 01:48.441
Keep an eye on your surroundings for now.

22
01:48.525 --> 01:50.110
I'll handle things here.

23
01:52.112 --> 01:53.822
-Mario! -Mario!

24
01:53.905 --> 01:54.864
Mario, there's a fire!

25
01:54.948 --> 01:56.366
Come on, let's go!

26
01:57.033 --> 01:58.201
Hurry up!

27
01:58.284 --> 02:00.411
-Faster! -Sir Mario.

28
02:00.495 --> 02:01.329
Where?

29
02:01.412 --> 02:03.498
-Over there! -Hurry!

30
02:03.581 --> 02:04.833
Let's get out!

31
02:04.916 --> 02:06.251
-Bags. -Quick!

32
02:06.334 --> 02:07.961
-What's the update? -Mar.

33
02:08.044 --> 02:10.672
Looks like the portable fan overheated.

34
02:10.755 --> 02:12.549
Good thing we noticed it right away,

35
02:12.632 --> 02:14.092
so the fire didn't spread.

36
02:14.676 --> 02:16.261
It was pretty close to our house, too.

37
02:16.344 --> 02:17.929
My buzz is gone.

38
02:18.012 --> 02:20.098
I got really scared, Mario.

39
02:20.181 --> 02:22.183
Thank God no one got hurt, right?

40
02:22.267 --> 02:23.309
Exactly.

41
02:24.018 --> 02:25.103
Okay, Mar.

42
02:25.812 --> 02:26.938
We'll double-check the area first.

43
02:27.021 --> 02:27.856
Okay, okay. Thanks.

44
02:30.275 --> 02:31.151
Come out!

45
02:31.234 --> 02:32.318
Hurry.

46
02:34.737 --> 02:35.655
Mario.

47
02:36.239 --> 02:38.408
Good thing it was just a small fire.

48
02:38.491 --> 02:40.410
I thought there was another Manananggal.

49
02:42.162 --> 02:44.164
But this isn't an isolated incident.

50
02:45.331 --> 02:47.250
Especially now that there's someone lurking around,

51
02:47.333 --> 02:50.003
that vigilante you call a Manananggal.

52
02:50.837 --> 02:52.630
But we've been through this before.

53
02:53.131 --> 02:54.173
In Cebu.

54
02:54.257 --> 02:57.635
Remember how it started small, then got worse over time?

55
02:58.303 --> 03:00.638
But, Captain Pepe, maybe tomorrow,

56
03:01.222 --> 03:03.057
you can start patrolling again.

57
03:03.808 --> 03:05.310
Not because we're panicking.

58
03:05.393 --> 03:07.604
We just want to make sure we're safe.

59
03:08.187 --> 03:10.273
-Yes, Mario. -We're game!

60
03:13.902 --> 03:15.236
Wait, one more thing.

61
03:16.029 --> 03:17.155
As much as possible,

62
03:17.238 --> 03:19.991
don't tell anyone about this. Not a soul.

63
03:20.074 --> 03:21.743
Especially Chiara and Mikoy.

64
03:22.785 --> 03:23.995
They already have enough on their plate.

65
03:24.078 --> 03:25.747
We don't need to add to it.

66
03:25.830 --> 03:29.000
-You heard what Mario said. -These two are such gossips.

67
03:29.083 --> 03:31.044
Yes, sir. Yes, Mario.

68
03:31.127 --> 03:32.295
Yes? You two gossips?

69
03:32.378 --> 03:34.130
-No, sir. -We're just drunk.

70
03:37.383 --> 03:38.843
Oh, gosh.

71
04:00.490 --> 04:02.742
Here's your water bottle, sweetheart.

72
04:02.825 --> 04:04.869
I didn't wake you up early

73
04:04.953 --> 04:06.204
because I thought,

74
04:06.287 --> 04:09.040
of course, my future wife needs her beauty rest.

75
04:09.123 --> 04:11.125
We wouldn't want her turning into a beast, right?

76
04:17.131 --> 04:19.676
My sweetheart is so sweet. He even got me

77
04:20.260 --> 04:22.887
a tumbler.

78
04:22.971 --> 04:24.806
You remind me of someone

79
04:25.431 --> 04:26.683
I used to date

80
04:27.767 --> 04:29.269
-in Hong Kong. -Huh?

81
04:29.978 --> 04:31.437
Dasho.

82
04:40.989 --> 04:42.573
You know, I know him too.

83
04:43.199 --> 04:45.785
I know he's handsome and quite the catch,

84
04:45.868 --> 04:46.911
that Dasho.

85
04:47.662 --> 04:50.540
Yes, he's kind of like Mr. Suave.

86
04:52.625 --> 04:54.502
Thank you, sweetheart,

87
04:55.837 --> 04:59.215
for taking care of me and for everything.

88
05:04.304 --> 05:05.471
There you go.

89
05:06.347 --> 05:07.849
Why are you being so sweet today, sweetheart?

90
05:07.932 --> 05:08.975
What's the occasion?

91
05:09.892 --> 05:11.436
You want something again, don't you?

92
05:12.687 --> 05:14.397
What could my sweetheart possibly want?

93
05:17.775 --> 05:19.902
-You idiot! -Why?

94
05:20.486 --> 05:21.821
I'm just kidding.

95
05:26.451 --> 05:28.244
I was just thinking.

96
05:33.207 --> 05:35.626
What if we don't go through with the wedding?

97
05:49.140 --> 05:50.224
Dara.

98
05:50.308 --> 05:51.434
Dara!

99
05:52.852 --> 05:54.187
Look.

100
05:54.270 --> 05:58.191
Sean looked like such an idiot. He was so drunk at the bridal shower.

101
05:59.067 --> 06:02.320
Carlota, I was there. I saw it in person.

102
06:03.946 --> 06:05.114
Were you there?

103
06:05.698 --> 06:08.618
Yes. You're just so whipped.

104
06:08.701 --> 06:12.330
You don't notice anything else except that Sianong.

105
06:13.748 --> 06:14.832
Well,

106
06:14.916 --> 06:18.211
if by whipped, you mean head over heels,

107
06:19.212 --> 06:20.838
then yes.

108
06:20.922 --> 06:24.634
I'm head over heels in love with him.

109
06:24.717 --> 06:25.885
Anyway,

110
06:25.968 --> 06:28.054
look at this. Here.

111
06:28.137 --> 06:29.472
This is my favorite!

112
06:30.473 --> 06:32.433
There! Look.

113
06:36.646 --> 06:38.022
Why do you look like you didn't sleep?

114
06:39.023 --> 06:39.941
I didn't.

115
06:41.150 --> 06:42.777
Sean kept me up all night.

116
06:47.156 --> 06:51.035
Wait, wait. What does TMI mean?

117
06:51.119 --> 06:52.662
I don't want to talk about it.

118
06:52.745 --> 06:53.913
I don't want to talk about it.

119
06:56.791 --> 06:59.335
That's not what it means.

120
06:59.418 --> 07:00.294
No.

121
07:00.962 --> 07:03.506
I mean, I have some intel.

122
07:09.637 --> 07:12.390
I mean, we're still getting married.

123
07:16.936 --> 07:19.063
It'll be simpler, more intimate.

124
07:19.147 --> 07:21.691
Fewer…

125
07:23.860 --> 07:25.027
Fewer what?

126
07:27.488 --> 07:30.533
Fewer preparations.

127
07:30.616 --> 07:31.868
Right?

128
07:31.951 --> 07:33.494
It'll be cheaper, too.

129
07:33.578 --> 07:34.495
Think about it.

130
07:37.498 --> 07:38.499
Come here.

131
07:40.376 --> 07:41.502
Look at me.

132
07:46.382 --> 07:48.092
We're going through with the wedding.

133
07:49.844 --> 07:51.471
We're having the church wedding,

134
07:51.554 --> 07:53.431
we're having the reception,

135
07:53.514 --> 07:57.143
and yes, we're doing our dance numbers, too. Okay?

136
07:59.437 --> 08:01.731
I know you want everything to be simple,

137
08:02.523 --> 08:05.735
but I also know that's not really the reason.

138
08:09.739 --> 08:12.867
I know you're worried that your mom and dad won't be able to make it.

139
08:15.661 --> 08:17.038
I'm worried about that too, sweetheart.

140
08:17.747 --> 08:20.082
Of course, I'm sad that they won't be there, too.

141
08:21.626 --> 08:23.878
Because I want them to see you walk down the aisle.

142
08:25.588 --> 08:27.548
I want them to see your smile

143
08:28.508 --> 08:30.301
as you walk toward the altar.

144
08:31.135 --> 08:31.969
Right?

145
08:34.514 --> 08:38.267
And of course, I want to hear your dad say,

146
08:47.652 --> 08:49.570
just because they're not here

147
08:50.321 --> 08:51.989
doesn't mean we shouldn't have a wedding.

148
08:53.533 --> 08:56.035
If anything, I think we should go through with it even more.

149
08:56.118 --> 08:57.453
Yes.

150
08:57.537 --> 08:59.205
So that someday,

151
08:59.288 --> 09:01.958
when we're finally reunited with them,

152
09:02.583 --> 09:04.210
we can be proud that

153
09:04.293 --> 09:08.172
we still made their dream come true, of a happy life for you.

154
09:10.007 --> 09:10.967
Right?

155
09:12.176 --> 09:13.261
And one more thing, sweetheart.

156
09:13.344 --> 09:16.097
So many people helped us get this far.

157
09:17.098 --> 09:18.391
This wedding

158
09:18.474 --> 09:20.643
isn't just a celebration for the two of us.

159
09:20.726 --> 09:23.062
It's also our way of saying thank you

160
09:23.145 --> 09:25.690
to everyone who loved us and helped us along the way.

161
09:29.026 --> 09:30.653
Oh, and sweetheart,

162
09:30.736 --> 09:33.114
we've already paid our suppliers so much.

163
09:33.197 --> 09:34.240
What a waste!

164
09:34.323 --> 09:35.533
Oh my!

165
09:35.616 --> 09:37.201
I thought you were being serious.

166
09:37.285 --> 09:38.619
I am serious, sweetheart.

167
09:39.203 --> 09:42.164
I'm just being practical, right?

168
09:44.208 --> 09:45.293
But wait.

169
09:45.793 --> 09:46.919
Why?

170
09:48.754 --> 09:52.550
Did you get a last-minute love confession?

171
09:52.633 --> 09:54.343
Is someone trying to steal you away?

172
09:54.427 --> 09:57.179
Hey! If there is, let them come out.

173
09:57.722 --> 09:59.223
-What? -Sweetheart.

174
09:59.307 --> 10:00.808
They can all keep quiet forever.

175
10:02.351 --> 10:03.894
You guys are something else.

176
10:12.820 --> 10:15.531
Did you hear about what happened to Ma'am's husband?

177
10:16.198 --> 10:17.366
The one who used to be here?

178
10:17.450 --> 10:19.827
The bald guy, Viktor Valtrovi?

179
10:19.910 --> 10:22.580
Yes. Apparently, he got badly beaten up.

180
10:22.663 --> 10:24.749
They even had to take him to the clinic last night.

181
10:24.832 --> 10:26.417
What happened? Was there a riot?

182
10:27.501 --> 10:29.086
It's still unclear.

183
10:29.170 --> 10:31.464
All they said was he could barely stand.

184
10:31.547 --> 10:34.008
I think we made the wrong call letting him stay here.

185
10:34.091 --> 10:35.468
HQ is going to come after us for this.

186
10:35.551 --> 10:37.261
General Norberto might find out.

187
10:37.845 --> 10:38.679
Let's go.

188
10:50.107 --> 10:53.027
Word is Viktor underwent a medical exam.

189
10:54.612 --> 10:55.988
Why?

190
10:59.033 --> 11:01.077
Because of the severity of his injuries.

191
11:01.160 --> 11:02.328
Injuries?

192
11:04.205 --> 11:05.373
How is he?

193
11:06.957 --> 11:07.958
It's still unclear.

194
11:09.752 --> 11:11.379
There's no conclusive report yet.

195
11:12.797 --> 11:17.676
We still don't know if there was a fight or if he committed some violation inside.

196
11:20.388 --> 11:21.514
Hold on.

197
11:21.597 --> 11:25.684
Carlota, why do you seem so concerned about Viktor?

198
11:25.768 --> 11:29.897
Wasn't he the one who wanted to have you killed?

199
11:31.107 --> 11:32.024
Yes.

200
11:33.275 --> 11:37.113
But that doesn't mean we both have to be bad people.

201
11:37.780 --> 11:39.031
Besides,

202
11:42.368 --> 11:43.494
But

203
11:44.161 --> 11:46.288
I feel even worse for Chiara.

204
11:47.289 --> 11:48.999
You're worried about Chiara too?

205
11:49.083 --> 11:50.543
I thought you two weren't on good terms.

206
11:52.002 --> 11:53.129
That was before.

207
11:53.838 --> 11:56.298
But she's different now.

208
11:59.969 --> 12:03.722
And she's no longer the hot-headed assassin she used to be.

209
12:04.306 --> 12:06.809
Carlota, do you have a fever?

210
12:07.476 --> 12:10.438
You're worried about two people who wanted to kill you?

211
12:19.238 --> 12:22.324
Maybe we can talk to General Norberto?

212
12:27.538 --> 12:28.747
There's an update.

213
12:31.876 --> 12:33.169
No special permit.

214
12:35.045 --> 12:38.382
Viktor and Donabel won't be able to attend the wedding.

215
12:48.893 --> 12:51.312
Chiara, Mikoy, dinner's ready!

216
12:51.395 --> 12:53.189
Come out already!

217
12:53.689 --> 12:56.150
-Hey, Vicky, I have a question for you. -Go ahead.

218
12:56.233 --> 12:58.861
Are Italian men sweet?

219
12:59.445 --> 13:01.697
-At first. -But?

220
13:02.364 --> 13:04.950
Once football comes into the picture,

221
13:05.034 --> 13:06.660
you won't have a husband anymore.

222
13:10.331 --> 13:12.708
Well, I never married an Italian.

223
13:12.791 --> 13:14.627
I just heard those stories

224
13:14.710 --> 13:17.880
from my friends and colleagues who married Italians.

225
13:17.963 --> 13:19.757
That's where I heard them.

226
13:20.841 --> 13:22.176
Okay, one more question.

227
13:22.259 --> 13:23.928
If you had to choose,

228
13:27.598 --> 13:28.474
Depends.

229
13:29.475 --> 13:30.476
On what?

230
13:30.559 --> 13:33.729
On who knows how to wash the dishes.

231
13:34.730 --> 13:37.191
Good answer! You know my Mario?

232
13:37.274 --> 13:40.069
I was the one who taught him. Yes.

233
13:40.653 --> 13:42.404
So, Mikoy,

234
13:42.488 --> 13:44.990
do you know how to wash the dishes?

235
13:45.074 --> 13:47.993
Oh, really! Me? Of course I do!

236
13:48.077 --> 13:49.662
I know how to wash the dishes,

237
13:49.745 --> 13:52.122
iron, sweep, and do the laundry.

238
13:52.206 --> 13:55.668
I even know how to bake. I can do a somersault and shake my hips.

239
13:55.751 --> 13:58.629
Wow! Well, well, well.

240
13:58.712 --> 14:02.132
My girl really is lucky to have you!

241
14:02.216 --> 14:04.343
Oh, very lucky, Mama Vicky.

242
14:04.426 --> 14:06.720
I've truly been blessed with him.

243
14:09.056 --> 14:11.809
You two became such close friends so quickly!

244
14:12.434 --> 14:14.186
Tell me about it!

245
14:14.270 --> 14:15.271
You know, I feel like

246
14:15.354 --> 14:18.065
we've been friends for so long already.

247
14:18.148 --> 14:20.317
Right? And because of that,

248
14:21.193 --> 14:22.945
I have an idea, kids.

249
14:24.405 --> 14:28.701
Because, your Ninang Mylene won't be able to make it to your wedding

250
14:28.784 --> 14:30.160
because of a family emergency…

251
14:30.911 --> 14:35.457
It's such a shame, yes, but I guess it's a blessing in disguise.

252
14:35.541 --> 14:36.667
Why?

253
14:38.002 --> 14:43.716
Because Vicky has agreed to be your wedding godmother.

254
14:43.799 --> 14:44.884
Yes!

255
14:46.051 --> 14:47.469
-Really? -Yes!

256
14:50.055 --> 14:51.056
Thank you so much!

257
14:53.934 --> 14:54.810
Mommy Vicky.

258
14:54.894 --> 14:57.354
I'm just a little embarrassed because

259
14:57.438 --> 14:59.815
we don't really know each other that well yet.

260
15:00.482 --> 15:01.817
For now.

261
15:01.901 --> 15:05.070
Don't worry. We'll get to know each other better.

262
15:05.154 --> 15:07.448
I still have plenty of time to keep an eye on you

263
15:07.531 --> 15:11.452
and see if you're really perfect for my girl.

264
15:11.535 --> 15:13.746
Yes, ma'am.

265
15:14.246 --> 15:16.332
Behave yourself, Mikoy.

266
15:18.083 --> 15:18.918
Let's eat.

267
15:20.169 --> 15:21.045
Let's eat.

268
15:24.006 --> 15:25.257
This smells good.

269
15:27.426 --> 15:28.427
So sweet!

270
15:40.105 --> 15:41.774
I thought you were the bride.

271
15:42.608 --> 15:44.151
Why are you sneaking away?

272
15:45.277 --> 15:46.862
I am the bride,

273
15:46.946 --> 15:48.447
not a hostage.

274
15:52.326 --> 15:53.786
How are they?

275
15:54.578 --> 15:55.537
Well…

276
15:56.372 --> 15:57.831
Last I heard,

277
15:58.582 --> 16:00.584
your mom is still as stubborn as ever,

278
16:01.168 --> 16:03.337
and your dad is even more stubborn.

279
16:08.842 --> 16:12.012
It's scarier when Dad is nice.

280
16:12.596 --> 16:15.099
It's even scarier when you're nice to me.

281
16:19.603 --> 16:23.399
Well, there's been a little character development.

282
16:23.482 --> 16:27.152
The former hot-headed brat I knew

283
16:27.236 --> 16:32.533
is now a slightly less hot-headed country girl.

284
16:34.451 --> 16:37.579
Well, it's easier to breathe in the fresh air here.

285
16:37.663 --> 16:43.711
And it's refreshing to have clean and clear life intentions.

286
16:45.546 --> 16:46.380
What?

287
16:47.089 --> 16:48.340
Are you ready?

288
16:53.721 --> 16:54.763
I'm ready.

289
16:58.058 --> 16:59.059
I just hope…

290
17:01.103 --> 17:04.857
Let's hope Viktor and Donabel can make it.

291
17:11.071 --> 17:12.531
Besides,

292
17:12.614 --> 17:15.242
it would be a shame if they couldn't make it, right?

293
17:15.909 --> 17:17.536
You're their only daughter, after all.

294
17:21.790 --> 17:24.418
It would be perfect if they could make it.

295
17:25.002 --> 17:26.253
You know what?

296
17:26.336 --> 17:28.380
Let's manifest it.

297
17:33.802 --> 17:35.262
Wait a minute.

298
17:35.345 --> 17:38.682
I thought our relationship was leveling up.

299
17:38.766 --> 17:40.017
Why am I still a Chihuahua?

300
17:52.237 --> 17:54.156
Come on. Let's go inside.

301
17:54.239 --> 17:55.908
They're waiting for you.

302
18:03.415 --> 18:06.085
Hey, what are you doing?

303
18:06.168 --> 18:07.544
You look like you're deep in thought.

304
18:07.628 --> 18:09.630
You've been stirring that coffee for three hours.

305
18:11.632 --> 18:12.508
Cocoy.

306
18:14.134 --> 18:16.261
What if we help Viktor?

307
18:17.054 --> 18:18.722
How do we help Viktor?

308
18:20.432 --> 18:21.266
We break him out.

309
18:22.643 --> 18:23.477
What?

310
18:25.187 --> 18:26.438
It will be quick.

311
18:27.064 --> 18:28.607
We'll just get him out,

312
18:29.274 --> 18:31.527
then bring him back after the wedding.

313
18:32.361 --> 18:34.154
Like we're just borrowing him.

314
18:35.781 --> 18:37.241
Come on, Carlota.

315
18:38.242 --> 18:43.705
Viktor is a person, not something that you can return after borrowing.

316
18:45.165 --> 18:46.166
Then,

317
18:50.337 --> 18:51.255
Look.

318
18:51.338 --> 18:53.966
Do you really think that if Viktor escapes,

319
18:54.800 --> 18:55.717
he'll come back?

320
18:58.053 --> 18:59.429
I'm just worried.

321
19:00.639 --> 19:01.557
Something's wrong.

322
19:27.708 --> 19:30.544
But I have a crush on you.

323
19:31.712 --> 19:33.255
I have a crush on you too.

324
19:33.338 --> 19:35.132
So we're crushiecakes now?

325
19:40.220 --> 19:42.222
Is it still replaying in your head?

326
19:45.642 --> 19:46.727
Alex.

327
19:47.477 --> 19:48.770
Is it that obvious?

328
19:49.813 --> 19:50.856
Very.

329
19:53.233 --> 19:56.528
Can't we just erase whatever happened that night?

330
19:57.279 --> 19:59.448
We can't. It's already written.

331
20:01.533 --> 20:03.285
You know, Alex, you know how

332
20:03.368 --> 20:05.829
I confessed while I was drunk,

333
20:05.913 --> 20:08.040
and then we even got married?

334
20:08.749 --> 20:11.210
Doesn't that make me seem so easy?

335
20:12.252 --> 20:13.295
It's embarrassing.

336
20:14.671 --> 20:17.257
Now that you've finally said how you really feel,

337
20:18.634 --> 20:21.053
I mean, you're free now.

338
20:21.136 --> 20:22.137
You've already won.

339
20:22.221 --> 20:23.722
Not because you'll end up together.

340
20:23.805 --> 20:25.515
You've won because

341
20:25.599 --> 20:28.310
you're no longer lying about how you really feel.

342
20:28.393 --> 20:31.063
And you don't have anything to hide anymore.

343
20:31.772 --> 20:33.023
That's true.

344
20:33.106 --> 20:35.859
It's just really hard to repress your feelings.

345
20:35.943 --> 20:38.612
You know, it's kind of constipating?

346
20:39.404 --> 20:40.572
Isn't that true?

347
20:40.656 --> 20:42.366
Oh, Sofie.

348
20:43.242 --> 20:44.826
Right, Alex?

349
20:44.910 --> 20:45.869
Do you get what I mean?

350
20:47.788 --> 20:50.958
Well, if those hidden feelings are stressing you out,

351
20:51.708 --> 20:53.043
then yes,

352
20:53.126 --> 20:54.753
it can affect your gut health.

353
20:55.587 --> 20:58.548
But if you both feel the same way,

354
20:58.632 --> 20:59.716
then that's good.

355
20:59.800 --> 21:02.177
I think you'll be fine.

356
21:02.803 --> 21:04.638
You even got married, right?

357
21:08.141 --> 21:10.352
But wasn't he drunk too?

358
21:12.604 --> 21:14.481
Well, if he wasn't,

359
21:14.564 --> 21:16.650
at least you're free to move forward now.

360
21:20.070 --> 21:20.904
You're right.

361
21:21.697 --> 21:22.531
You're right.

362
21:23.115 --> 21:24.783
I've said what I needed to say.

363
21:24.866 --> 21:26.702
Now, it's up to him.

364
21:45.929 --> 21:47.014
Chiara.

365
21:47.097 --> 21:48.348
Are you okay?

366
21:49.016 --> 21:51.101
Yes, Mom. I'm okay.

367
21:52.269 --> 21:56.815
I thought you were upset because I made Vicky your wedding godmother.

368
21:58.191 --> 21:59.651
No, Mom.

369
22:01.028 --> 22:04.156
I was just surprised, but of course, I'm happy because

370
22:04.239 --> 22:07.701
I never thought Mama Yaya and I would see each other again.

371
22:10.287 --> 22:13.248
You two really clicked so quickly, the two of you.

372
22:13.332 --> 22:14.458
I know, right?

373
22:14.541 --> 22:19.087
You know, it's like because we've become such good friends,

374
22:19.171 --> 22:21.173
she feels like the sister I never had.

375
22:21.923 --> 22:23.717
You have a missing sister?

376
22:23.800 --> 22:25.886
No, hello.

377
22:25.969 --> 22:27.179
It just feels that way.

378
22:27.804 --> 22:28.805
Yes.

379
22:29.306 --> 22:33.769
You know, I really hope they allow your mom to come here.

380
22:33.852 --> 22:35.854
Then the three of us will be complete.

381
22:35.937 --> 22:39.900
Rosario, Rosenda, and Rosemarie.

382
22:41.485 --> 22:42.527
Who are they?

383
22:42.611 --> 22:44.780
Why, the three Claudines!

384
22:47.282 --> 22:49.493
Maybe you weren't even born back then!

385
22:49.576 --> 22:50.702
Wait a minute.

386
22:51.244 --> 22:52.788
What do you mean?

387
22:53.789 --> 22:55.999
We'll just be the Powerpuff Girls. I'm Bubbles.

388
22:57.292 --> 23:00.587
Perfect. Mama Yaya and I both love Blossom.

389
23:00.670 --> 23:04.341
Then Donabel can be Buttercup.

390
23:04.424 --> 23:06.176
She's the hothead, after all.

391
23:06.259 --> 23:07.385
Doesn't that fit?

392
23:08.804 --> 23:11.139
I hope they get approved.

393
23:11.223 --> 23:12.265
Oh, dear.

394
23:12.349 --> 23:13.475
If that happens,

395
23:13.558 --> 23:15.143
poor Mario.

396
23:15.227 --> 23:17.854
We'll all be bossing him around at the same time.

397
23:32.369 --> 23:35.455
Auntie Mercy, maybe we can get

398
23:35.539 --> 23:37.082
a future-husband discount here!

399
23:37.165 --> 23:37.999
There you go!

400
23:38.083 --> 23:40.836
A discount! Perfect timing. I'm vlogging her!

401
23:40.919 --> 23:42.045
Come on.

402
23:43.755 --> 23:45.132
-Perfect timing. He's vlogging. -You're something else, Mikoy.

403
23:45.215 --> 23:47.551
Fine, just add these two pieces.

404
23:47.634 --> 23:48.635
-Yes! -Yes!

405
23:48.718 --> 23:49.803
Thank you, Mommy Mercy!

406
23:49.886 --> 23:50.971
Thank you!

407
23:51.054 --> 23:52.973
-There you go. Thank you! -Thank you!

408
23:53.849 --> 23:55.517
You're really good at this, Mikoy!

409
23:55.600 --> 23:56.852
Of course!

410
24:00.272 --> 24:01.690
Bro.

411
24:02.482 --> 24:03.483
Thank you.

412
24:05.652 --> 24:06.611
For what?

413
24:06.695 --> 24:07.821
For Mom.

414
24:08.905 --> 24:12.159
I didn't expect you guys to accept her like that.

415
24:13.618 --> 24:14.953
Why wouldn't we?

416
24:15.036 --> 24:16.997
You're important to us.

417
24:17.080 --> 24:19.207
So naturally, she's important to us too.

418
24:19.291 --> 24:20.333
Really?

419
24:21.418 --> 24:22.919
Because, Bro,

420
24:23.003 --> 24:24.921
she just showed up out of nowhere, and then

421
24:25.005 --> 24:26.047
she's already the godmother.

422
24:28.133 --> 24:29.843
I was surprised too.

423
24:29.926 --> 24:32.304
But look at her and Mom Tess, right?

424
24:32.387 --> 24:34.472
They act like they've been friends forever!

425
24:35.140 --> 24:38.894
And it's actually nice that she was Chiara's nanny.

426
24:39.728 --> 24:41.479
When you think about it,

427
24:42.063 --> 24:44.357
doesn't that mean you and Chiara are practically siblings now?

428
24:44.441 --> 24:45.525
Right?

429
24:46.193 --> 24:47.152
Exactly.

430
24:47.235 --> 24:49.738
And Chiara seems happy about it, right?

431
24:50.864 --> 24:52.157
Of course!

432
24:52.240 --> 24:53.992
Of course, and so am I.

433
24:54.576 --> 24:59.289
-I'm over the moon that my bride is happy. -Nice.

434
25:01.166 --> 25:02.000
Hey!

435
25:02.083 --> 25:03.501
-Where are you from? -I'm getting late.

436
25:03.585 --> 25:04.544
Where are you from?

437
25:04.628 --> 25:05.629
Not far.

438
25:05.712 --> 25:07.172
-All right. -Just on the corner of the street.

439
25:07.255 --> 25:08.590
-Okay, buddy, head on in. -Where is this located?

440
25:08.673 --> 25:10.383
Is this even Team Groom anymore?

441
25:10.926 --> 25:12.260
It's starting to look like a security agency.

442
25:12.344 --> 25:13.553
Let me take a look first.

443
25:13.637 --> 25:15.305
-How do you know him? -He's my brother.

444
25:15.388 --> 25:16.264
Okay, brother-in-law.

445
25:16.348 --> 25:17.599
-Sir. -Bro.

446
25:17.682 --> 25:20.644
-I go here frequently. -Could there be a reason for this?

447
25:21.603 --> 25:24.022
Wait, where are you heading? Stop.

448
25:24.105 --> 25:26.399
-What is that? -Let me take a look.

449
25:26.483 --> 25:29.236
Don't they seem a little too serious?

450
25:29.319 --> 25:30.779
-Keep going straight. -I need to hurry.

451
25:30.862 --> 25:33.281
Wait, Captain Pepe, Mario.

452
25:33.365 --> 25:34.574
What is this for?

453
25:34.658 --> 25:35.951
They weren't like this before.

454
25:54.803 --> 25:55.762
I totally knew that.

455
25:55.845 --> 25:58.848
Those moves are full of doubts.

456
25:58.932 --> 26:01.434
I know, because I used to be like that!

457
26:02.269 --> 26:04.104
Hang on. We have to take a selfie.

458
26:07.065 --> 26:09.484
We will make them jealous. We're all so pretty today.

459
26:09.567 --> 26:11.194
See? I'm going to send this to him.

460
26:11.278 --> 26:13.405
Look, Tess sent a groupie.

461
26:14.906 --> 26:17.117
We can't lose. Mikoy!

462
26:21.037 --> 26:21.955
Carlota?

463
26:22.956 --> 26:24.207
What are you doing here?

464
26:24.291 --> 26:26.334
Did Senator Quintin send you?

465
26:26.418 --> 26:28.003
If he's the one who sent me,

466
26:28.086 --> 26:30.880
I wouldn't give you a tissue. Donabel,

467
26:32.090 --> 26:33.049
Let's go.
